<h2 id="aprendizaje">What I learned <i class="fas fa-graduation-cap"></i> </h2>
<p>
  • Layered pattern — Why business rules go in <code>services/</code> and not in the routes or the models.<br />
  • Flask blueprints — Separating the API by domain instead of having a file that grows without control.<br />
  • Schema migrations — Versioning the database with Alembic instead of recreating it on every start.<br />
  • Sessions and authorization — Signed <code>HttpOnly</code> cookie + <code>SameSite=Lax</code>, and role guards on the server side.<br />
  • Design system with tokens — A single place defines light, dark and the colour of each role.<br />
  • Scoped tool calling — Giving the model read-only tools limited by role instead of free access to the database.<br />
  • Local RAG — ChromaDB and embeddings so the assistant answers with the sources the administrator uploads.<br />
  • Spec-driven pipeline — Twelve use cases closed with specification, tests, visual evidence and review before archiving.<br />
</p>